      "writtenOn": "2023-02-24T09:51:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This makes me think that the `onLost()` is not always fired when there is a new network. For example, if the device is connected to mobile data first, and then connects to Wi-Fi later, `onLost()` won\u0027t fire for this case. Vpn.java only receives `onAvailable()`.\n\n`onLost()` will be fired when both Wi-Fi and mobile data are connected, and the Wi-Fi is disconnected. For this case, `onLost()` will be fired for Wi-Fi, and `onAvailable()` will be fired for mobile data.\n\nI left a related comment in https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/2452265/4/services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Vpn.java#3425.",
